/// Date contains the calendar information used for time-based analysis of sales and business performance. Each row represents one calendar date. Date Key is the technical key used to connect dates to sales transactions. The table contains standard calendar attributes such as Date, Year, Quarter, Month, Month Number, Week, Day, Day Name, and weekend indicators where available. Use the Date table for all time-based analysis, filtering, grouping, and time-intelligence calculations rather than using raw date fields from the Sales table. The Date table is the primary calendar dimension for calculating monthly, quarterly, yearly, YTD, MTD, previous-period, and year-over-year sales metrics.
table Date
	lineageTag: 517a5aa6-038c-443a-a31c-33daac98f546
	sourceLineageTag: [gold].[dim_date]

	/// Technical integer key representing a calendar date in YYYYMMDD format. It is used to connect Sales transactions to the Date dimension and should normally be hidden from business users.
	column DateKey
		dataType: int64
		formatString: 0
		lineageTag: ef7d901b-81aa-4ab5-9afe-002e9edd1044
		sourceLineageTag: DateKey
		summarizeBy: none
